From: AD5X Open OS
Subject: [PATCH] net: ingenic mac: set_mac_address keeps dev_addr_shadow

ifconfig eth0 hw ether calls ndo_set_mac_address, which copied the new address
into dev_addr only. dev_addr_check() then warns "Incorrect netdev->dev_addr"
at every ifconfig up, because dev_addr_shadow still holds the random probe
address. dev_addr_set() writes both. Behaviour is otherwise unchanged.

--- a/module_drivers/drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/ingenic_mac.c
+++ b/module_drivers/drivers/net/ethernet/ingenic/ingenic_mac.c
@@ -2439,7 +2439,7 @@
 	if (netif_running(dev)) {
 		return -EBUSY;
 	}
-	memcpy((u8 *)dev->dev_addr, addr->sa_data, dev->addr_len);
+	dev_addr_set(dev, addr->sa_data);
 	setup_mac_addr(gmacdev, (u8 *)dev->dev_addr);
 	return 0;
 }
